amethyst (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Compound assignment (+= -= *= /= %=), len() builtin and a
    division/modulo-by-zero guard that exits with a runtime error.
  * Compiler warnings: unused variable and unreachable code, reported
    on stderr without stopping the build.
  * Array parameters passed as slices: int[] / bool[] (pointer + length),
    dynamic bounds checks and for i in 0..len(a).
  * string type: variables, parameters and returns, == / != compare
    contents, len() via strlen, print via puts.
  * float type: 64-bit IEEE 754 binary64 literals and arithmetic on SSE
    registers, explicit float(n) / int(x) conversions, print with %.15g.
  * Definite-assignment analysis: `var x: T;` may be left unassigned
    until every path that reads it has assigned it.
  * New examples: slices.amt, strings.amt, floats.amt, definite.amt.
  * Dev Kit Homepage now points at the actual repository.

 -- Amethyst Project <amethyst@localhost>  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000

amethyst (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Dev Kit release.
  * Ships amethystc (x86-64 GAS backend), amethyst-new helper,
    examples, templates, README and man pages.
  * Depends on gcc + binutils so beginners never build the compiler by hand.

 -- Amethyst Project <amethyst@localhost>  Mon, 22 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
